Part 1: What the brief gave us

The problem

The Growth team said: “Revenue dropped in September 2026 versus August 2026.”
The question: is it a real business change or a data problem?

The data

3 files: orders.csv, customers.csv, products.csv.
The files are deliberately messy, so we should not assume they are correct.

Finance rules we had to follow

Report August and September as two separate months.
Revenue = quantity × unit price, for completed orders only.
Exclude cancelled and refunded orders, and don’t subtract refunds.
Convert USD to INR at exactly ₹85. Other currencies are not supported unless we justify it.
Trim and lowercase the status. Don’t treat COMPLETE as completed.
Count only orders with a valid date, customer, product, positive quantity and positive price.
Remove exact duplicate rows. Quarantine conflicting rows with the same order ID.
New customer = first completed order in the Aug-Sep data. Later orders are repeat. State the limitation.

What we had to deliver

Data checks, a cleaned dataset with a rejected-rows log, SQL queries, a short summary, and AI verification.
Not graded: charts, slides, UI.
Part 2: What we found

Data problems

244 rows but only 240 unique order IDs (3 exact duplicates, plus O0089 conflicting).
Bad dates, blank and unknown customers, unknown products, zero or negative quantity, and zero price.
Wrong status values, plus 1 USD and 1 EUR row.
Result: 197 trusted orders.

Main answer

The revenue drop is real: ₹18.09 lakh to ₹11.37 lakh (−37%).

Why it dropped

Laptop 16 fell ₹7.92 lakh (13 units to 2 units). That is more than the whole net drop.
Laptop 14 rose ₹2.5 lakh, which reduced the drop a little.
Orders fell from 113 to 84, and the average order value fell from ₹16.0k to ₹13.5k.

Can the removed rows change the answer?

No. Rows that might have been revenue add only about ₹66k.

What we are not sure about

New vs repeat is only measured within Aug-Sep.
We don’t know why Laptop 16 sales fell, and we did not claim a cause.

Next action

Ask Sales whether August had big one-time Laptop 16 deals.
